31: *  today). A person's due-total is at most the cap (blank: none). A claim whose due is above the proof threshold in force on its date (blank: none) — its person's grade's own when one is in force then (dated like the floor; blank: none, so the sheet's) — is settled or approved only once it has a proof, and one whose due is above the note threshold in force on its date (blank: none) is opened only once it has a note. From the period numbering date on, an opened claim is numbered within its period (blank: off). Each grade may have grace days (blank: none), dated like the floor: a claim whose person's grade on its date has a grace in force on that date is overdue only once its due-by plus the grace is before the sheet's today, and its late charge counts from there; a blank grade's grace is saved as none when its from-date is given or it was the last field worked in. When the sheet's today is changed, each open period whose to-date plus the grace days is before it is closed (blank: off; not dated). While the entry date is set it is the date a new claim left undated is given (blank: off, the sheet's today; not dated).
